  <div class="new-box">
    <h4>▶ MULTI-BOWL DESIGN PHILOSOPHY — WHY MORE BOWLS</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>A single large flat boiler surface has diminishing returns — steam generated at one point has to travel through liquid to the steam space above, losing energy to the water column above it</li>
      <li>Multiple small hemispherical bowls each flash-convert their own localised water supply independently — the steam rises directly from the bowl surface into the steam space with no water column resistance above it</li>
      <li>Each bowl is a self-contained flash generator — fail one bowl and the rest continue — redundancy is built into the multi-bowl architecture at no extra cost</li>
      <li>Adding bowls adds steam output proportionally — the 100 gallon vessel can accommodate significantly more bowl surface area than the 14cm cube Aegis Boiler — exact bowl count to be confirmed in Phase 27 once vessel internal dimensions are confirmed in Blender</li>
      <li>Dome rivets on every bowl — uniform 5mm dome pattern — all Phase 23 bowl wisdom applied — water still has to flank the dome from the rear on every single rivet on every single bowl in the vessel</li>
      <li>TIG curved fillet on all interior vessel corners — even more critical at 100 gallon scale — larger vessel means larger corner stress under pressure cycling — fillets eliminate stress concentration at every corner</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

