      <li>At 900 RPM and 914mm stroke the piston mean speed is approximately 27.4 metres per second — this is above the typical locomotive limit of ~12 m/s but within the range of marine diesel pistons which reach 10–12 m/s — Phase 27 must confirm acceptable piston speed for the liner material and ring design chosen</li>
      <li>Cylinder barrel material: chromoly 4340 liner with chrome bore — same family as the Decker 9000 but scaled — bore finish to H7 tolerance — same honing spec applies at any diameter</li>
      <li>Crankshaft at 90 degrees confirmed carried from Decker 9000 — each locomotive wheel pair drives one crankshaft — crankshaft diameter must increase significantly from the 60mm 4340 used in the Decker — Phase 27 to calculate minimum crankshaft diameter at 200mm bore 500 PSI</li>
