<div class="panel" id="panel-trans">
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--tank)">Diagram 3 · Transmission — TBD Phase 27</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">Design Not Yet Started · Carrier Plate Concept · HTD V2 as Reference · Must Handle 42,000 Nm Idle Minimum</h2>
  <p class="section-lead">
    The Berserker transmission is not yet designed. This tab captures the known constraints, the carrier plate concept under consideration, and the HTD V2 from Phase 25 as a starting reference. Phase 27 will produce the full transmission design. The single firm constraint the Phase 27 design must satisfy is <strong style="color:var(--safe)">minimum rated torque of 42,000 Nm at idle (90 PSI)</strong> — rising to 234,000 Nm at maximum pressure. No conventional automotive or truck transmission can handle these loads. Like the Decker 9000, chain drive is the only viable approach at this torque scale.
    The <strong style="color:var(--tank)">carrier plate concept</strong> under consideration adapts the HTD telescopic derailleur concept to a much larger chain — multiple parallel chains per gear position, a large diameter carrier plate that holds multiple output sprockets at fixed radii, and a hydraulic actuator that indexes the entire carrier plate to bring successive sprocket rings into alignment with the input chain. This is analogous to an epicyclic gear carrier but using chain sprockets rather than planet gears.
  </p>

  <div class="metrics">
    <div class="metric"><div class="val" style="color:var(--tank)">TBD</div><div class="lbl">Transmission Design</div></div>
    <div class="metric"><div class="val" style="color:var(--safe)">42,000</div><div class="lbl">Min Nm  90 PSI</div></div>
