    <div class="metric"><div class="val" style="color:var(--muted)">PH27</div><div class="lbl">Design Phase</div></div>
  </div>

  <div class="new-box">
    <h4>▶ CARRIER PLATE CONCEPT — PRELIMINARY DESCRIPTION</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>A large diameter steel carrier plate — estimated 600–900mm diameter — is mounted on the transmission output shaft and can rotate freely relative to it until locked</li>
      <li>The carrier plate holds multiple concentric rings of sprocket teeth at different radii from the centre — each ring corresponds to one gear ratio — the different radii give different mechanical advantage</li>
      <li>The input chain from the engine crankshafts is always engaged with the currently selected sprocket ring — a hydraulic indexing actuator rotates the carrier plate to bring a new ring into alignment with the input chain</li>
      <li>When the desired ring is aligned the carrier plate locks to the output shaft via a hydraulic pin or jaw clutch — torque now flows from input chain through the selected ring through the locked carrier plate to the output shaft</li>
      <li>A clutch flywheel still disengages drive during indexing — same sequence as HTD V2 — the difference is the carrier plate rotates to the new position rather than a telescopic cylinder moving laterally</li>
      <li>This concept is more compact laterally than the HTD — the carrier plate keeps the chain on a single longitudinal plane — at Berserker scale lateral space in the chassis is limited and a single-plane transmission is preferred</li>
      <li>Multiple parallel chains per gear ring — to handle Berserker torque each sprocket ring may be driven by two or three parallel chains simultaneously — torque split across chains</li>
      <li>All details TBD Phase 27 — this is a concept description not a mechanical design — the Phase 27 Blender model will be the first engineering artefact for this system</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

