<div class="panel" id="panel-power">
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--elec)">Power and Torque Analysis — Phase 26 Estimates</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">Nm · Horsepower · Pressure Table · Comparison · Electrical System Scale</h2>
  <p class="section-lead">
    All figures below are estimates pending bore confirmation in Phase 27. The primary design assumption is <strong style="color:var(--safe)">200mm bore</strong> — two cylinders — 914mm stroke. Torque is calculated as: piston force × stroke arm (457mm) × 2 cylinders. Horsepower is calculated as: torque (ft-lbs) × RPM / 5252. Target operating RPM at cruise is 600–900 RPM. Peak HP is at maximum steam pressure and maximum sustainable RPM simultaneously. These are extraordinary numbers by any measure — the estimated peak of approximately 3,100 HP from two steam pistons fed by a 100 gallon multi-bowl boiler is comparable to four Bugatti Chirons combined and substantially exceeds any production diesel truck ever built.
  </p>

