  <div class="new-box">
    <h4>▶ ELECTRICAL SYSTEM — BERSERKER SCALE</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Alternator chain: multiple alternators required at Berserker scale — the 2× 2,500W dual alternator from the Decker 9000 is insufficient for the heater bank power draw at 100 gallon boiler scale</li>
      <li>Estimated heater bank for 100 gallon multi-bowl boiler: 20,000–40,000W depending on bowl count and target cold start time — this exceeds the alternator output significantly — large LiFePO4 battery bank required for cold start and low-RPM operations</li>
      <li>At cruise RPM 750+: alternator chain drives multiple large alternators off the crankshaft — 17.5:1 ratio maintained as starting reference — Phase 27 to calculate how many alternators and what kW rating to sustain the heater load during operation</li>
      <li>24V system remains the base bus for controls, solenoids, PID, and instrumentation — a dedicated 48V or 96V bus for heater elements is the likely Phase 27 recommendation given the heater power scale</li>
      <li>PID system upgrades needed: HTD/carrier plate gear position input, dual boiler EWI channels, dual exhaust valve channels per cylinder, dual oil temperature channels for dual tank belt housing — significantly more I/O than the Decker 9000 PID module</li>
    </ul>
