      <li>Task 3 — Design the carrier plate transmission — now that torque inputs are confirmed design the carrier plate: plate diameter, sprocket ring tooth counts for each gear, chain count per ring, hydraulic indexing actuator, clutch flywheel rated torque, Hall effect position sensors — produce the transmission Blender model</li>
      <li>Task 4 — Confirm dual tank belt chain spec — once transmission output torque per chain is confirmed, verify ANSI #160 DS safety factor holds — if not step up to ANSI #200 DS — confirm bevel gear tooth counts and rear differential selection</li>
      <li>Task 5 — Produce full Phase 27 parts list — every component with quantity, unit cost, total cost, weight — replace all Phase 26 estimates with confirmed specs — update total vehicle weight for Mack chassis</li>
    </ul>
