    <ul>
      <li>Bore must be confirmed and crankshaft geometry modelled at full scale before any machining is specified — every chain, every sprocket, every bearing, and the entire transmission derives from the bore figure</li>
      <li>Boiler pressure vessel must be designed by or reviewed by a qualified pressure vessel engineer before fabrication at 100 gallon scale at 500 PSI — this is not the 14cm Aegis Boiler Mark 1 — at this scale the regulatory and safety requirements for a pressure vessel of this volume at this pressure are significant</li>
      <li>Dual tank belt chain pull calculation must be confirmed at the Phase 27 bore — the ANSI #160 DS spec is the current best estimate, but if bore comes in larger than 200mm the chain must step up and the housing must be redesigned to match the larger chain pitch</li>
      <li>Carrier plate transmission must complete full bench test through all gear positions before installation — jam or mis-index on the Berserker with 42,000 Nm at idle is significantly more destructive than on the Decker 9000 — bench validation is non-negotiable</li>
      <li>All three oil compartment temperature and level sensors must be installed and verified before the vehicle moves under steam power — Berserker has more oil volume and more heat to manage than any previous Miasma platform</li>
